## Starting or adopting a project

Any project worth more than one session keeps a logbook.

**No `bitacora.config.json` in the repository?** Follow the `start-project`
skill before writing feature code — when starting something new, and equally
when the first request is a refactor, a migration, a cleanup before release, or
anything else that will not finish in one sitting. Do not wait to be asked:
being asked requires the person to already know the logbook exists, which is the
thing this rule exists to replace. The skill asks before adopting a repository
that has conventions of its own, so firing it is cheap and adoption is never
silent.

**Already has one?** The logs are not `@`-imported, so read them on demand —
`node .bitacora/cli.mjs recall <tag>` before writing a plan for an unfamiliar or
risky area, and log mistakes the moment they happen rather than at the end of
the session.
<!-- END:bitacora -->
